        "original_id": "c287b9fd-e5e5-53ba-9eb6-ac7a7587a169",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium, Platylobium infecundum\n- Families: Fabaceae, Iridaceae\n- People: James Edward Smith\n- Topics: plant taxonomy, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to the genus Bossiaea within the Mirbelioids.\n- Platylobium infecundum is a species in the genus Platylobium and the family Fabaceae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
